{"title":"A Winter Sky","artist":"George Inness (American, 1825–1894)","date":"1866","medium":"oil on canvas","classification":"Painting","styles":[],"subjects":[],"origin":"America","museum_caption":"In A Winter Sky , George Inness concentrated on depicting the effects of light and atmosphere. In this composition, the artist combined a vibrant, glowing sunset with a harsh, bleak landscape. Inness's color choice reinforces this contrast, as the warm pinks and yellows in the sky play off the cool blues of the frozen ground. Did you know? George Inness originally included a figure standing at the left edge of the pond, which he later painted over so that it is no longer visible."}

